20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405329#post1405329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think V20 was always meant to be a collector\u2019s edition more than an actual playable game.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the more expensive physical copies, yes they're for collectors, but V20's actually a really great update from the old 2nd ed/revised stuff with a little bit of streamlining and balance tweaks condensed into far fewer books than in earlier editions. I'm running games on it and prefer it to V5, which I'm not going to get into why here. At least the PDFs are reasonably cheap, but that high end V20 Dark Ages Vampire is really a beautiful book and was worth it for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:17:11-07:00","id":1405414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405404#post1405404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the more expensive physical copies, yes they're for collectors, but V20's actually a really great update from the old 2nd ed/revised stuff with a little bit of streamlining and balance tweaks condensed into far fewer books than in earlier editions. I'm running games on it and prefer it to V5, which I'm not going to get into why here. At least the PDFs are reasonably cheap, but that high end V20 Dark Ages Vampire is really a beautiful book and was worth it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I actually own the V20 PDF and I have played it. I just meant I thought originally V20 was intended for the collector\u2019s market and only later became a playable game with like sourcebooks and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T10:26:53-07:00","id":1405612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SavageGM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405322#post1405322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nah that\u2019s the deluxe one and it seems only ebay has that one. The premium one is the pod version with better color and thicker paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pity. I wanted one for my old Storyteller. I've tried Ebay, but it seems there are hoops before you can bid on things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T10:30:05-07:00","id":1405613,"title":"","content":"I do believe the reason is to push people to V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm","name":"SavageGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T11:21:00-07:00","id":1405628,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13440_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13440\" data-vbnamecard=\"13440\">SavageGM</a> maybe, but is that inherently a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Also, you can still buy the PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T12:27:12-07:00","id":1405648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405628#post1405628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13440_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13440\" data-vbnamecard=\"13440\">SavageGM</a> maybe, but is that inherently a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Also, you can still buy the PDF.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the consumer I think it is. Some people can\u2019t pay the price of premium and getting groups to buy their own books is already an obstacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm","name":"SavageGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T12:35:04-07:00","id":1405651,"title":"","content":"Okay. I get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:48:32-07:00","id":1405771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405628#post1405628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13440_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13440\" data-vbnamecard=\"13440\">SavageGM</a> maybe, but is that inherently a bad thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>From a purely business perspective, no, it's almost completely fine. Sabotaging an old product to boost sales for the one that's currently carrying your brand image is a savvy tactic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you can still buy the PDF. </div> </div> </div>PDF's are the future.<br /> But so is piracy.<br /> <br /> It'd be quite interesting to see a &quot;pay what you want&quot; scheme for digital copies. For the scheme itself and what it tells us about the quality of products involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T14:32:25-07:00","id":1405832,"title":"","content":"I've seen someone mention online that it might be a temporary thing. That its cause they're currently changing the book so it no longer contains the Lasombra portrait. Allegedly the guy in that photo recently turned out to be a creep of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T14:54:55-07:00","id":1405837,"title":"","content":"A RL creep playing a lasombra is not a problem. I'm more bothered by the lasombra illustration on the clan page. That sideboob is nightmare fuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T00:37:03-07:00","id":1405893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405837#post1405837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A RL creep playing a lasombra is not a problem. I'm more bothered by the lasombra illustration on the clan page. That sideboob is nightmare fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, the sideboob's not that big a deal, nothing you couldn't see on cable even back in the '90s, Vampire's always had some level of erotic art and some of the material's been graphic or shown full frontal (Remember the back cover of the original clanbook Tzimisce?). I've got more of a dislike for the art style that's been permeated in Revised and V20. The V20 Dark Ages art style is much more serious and less cartoony. As a fan of the old 2nd ed art, the V20 Dark Ages style really appeals to me a lot more than the modern setting V20 stuff. The artist being a creep's really a bigger deal, but I don't know the whole story behind that. I'm not a fan of the photo art from V5, either. For me, the old school 2nd ed stuff had the best art, even if most of it was black and white. It was more realistic and visceral. And if I had an IRL creep in my group, I'd tell them not to come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:43:39-07:00","id":1405931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405893#post1405893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh, the sideboob's not that big a deal, nothing you couldn't see on cable even back in the '90s, Vampire's always had some level of erotic art and some of the material's been graphic or shown full frontal (Remember the back cover of the original clanbook Tzimisce?). I've got more of a dislike for the art style that's been permeated in Revised and V20. The V20 Dark Ages art style is much more serious and less cartoony. As a fan of the old 2nd ed art, the V20 Dark Ages style really appeals to me a lot more than the modern setting V20 stuff. The artist being a creep's really a bigger deal, but I don't know the whole story behind that. I'm not a fan of the photo art from V5, either. For me, the old school 2nd ed stuff had the best art, even if most of it was black and white. It was more realistic and visceral. And if I had an IRL creep in my group, I'd tell them not to come back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you about the creep. And I liked the art in Fall of London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T00:04:31-07:00","id":1406071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405931#post1405931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you about the creep. And I liked the art in Fall of London.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually still haven't seen it, what's the style like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:39:25-07:00","id":1406098,"title":"","content":"Very old-school Gothic. Lots of rose and chalice imagery, lots of red and black (blood and shadows). Some cool club scenes. The character portraits are very moody and atmospheric. Really captures the feel of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T13:31:45-07:00","id":1410383,"title":"","content":"A cheaper version is available again: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/94815/Vampire-The-Masquerade-20th-Anniversary-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ersary-Edition</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T14:41:13-07:00","id":1410398,"title":"","content":"It seems that the Standard edition is still not made available again. Luckily for me, I managed to get one along with the whole V20 line when I dropped $442.80 in a single, one day purchase two years ago...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T16:37:54-07:00","id":1410427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404774-v20-only-premium-hardcover-available-on-drivethrurpg-for-v20?p=1405832#post1405832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen someone mention online that it might be a temporary thing. That its cause they're currently changing the book so it no longer contains the Lasombra portrait. Allegedly the guy in that photo recently turned out to be a creep of some kind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is true and it is why the books were pulled and various art and some context is being replaced before they will be available for reprint. Apparently the guy was a real creep. Onyx path is responding very seriously and responsibly supporting the ongoing fight to ride the world of people like that and they should be commended for it, but it does present a challenge to get the book.<br /> <br /> On the bright side there will be new art for a updated V20 book so that's kind of cool if you think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24511-xguild","name":"xguild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}